.claude/
.DS_Store

# Source art and working files. These are kept on disk but never deployed:
# The host serves everything in the repo whether or not a page links to it,
# and design sources carry metadata that a rendered asset does not need.
images/inv *
images/og-pose.png
images/logo.svg
images/os/icybearos.svg
images/os/icybearos.png
# the original wordmark save; the png is smaller and is what ships
icybearfun.svg

# Superseded by .webp (74% smaller, alpha bit-identical, no banding). Kept on
# disk as the lossless source but never deployed.
images/os/icy-stand-*.png
images/os/icy-sit*.png
images/os/icy-lock.png
images/os/icy-wawa.png
images/os/icy-avatar.png
images/os/icy-avatar2.png
images/os/mobile-lockscreen.png
# the heart Icy drew, traced into geometry by test/icons.py; the png is the source
images/os/icons/heart.png

# Superseded, and nothing links to them. Kept on disk, off the site.
#
# WHY THESE WERE STILL SHIPPING. Listing a path here does nothing to a file git
# is already tracking -- the rule only decides what git picks up NEXT. Several
# of the entries above had been written and never followed with an untrack, so
# 51.6MB sat in the repo under an ignore rule that read as if it had handled it.
# If a file is added here and it is already committed, it has to be untracked in
# the same pass: git rm --cached -- <path>
#
# the site links favicon-16/32/48/180; these two are from an older set
images/favicon.png
images/favicon-512.png
# POSES loads icy-sit-1..5. This one is not in the sequence and never loads.
images/os/icy-sit-sleep.webp
# os.css masks images/os/icybearos-sm.png, which is a different file
images/os/icybearfun-sm.png
# only test/og-image.html draws it, and test/ is not deployed
images/logo.png

# Working files that should not be versioned at all. These are different from
# the _config.yml exclude list: that one keeps things out of the published
# site, this keeps them out of the repo entirely.
#
# Note: '#' only opens a comment at the START of a line here. A trailing one
# becomes part of the pattern and the rule silently matches nothing.

# one-off CORS probe against the edge functions
_cors_probe.html
# a debug capture of the share card
card-base-day-full.png
# Figma's export name; icybear-cv.pdf is the identical file that ships
CV - Icy.pdf

# Visual regression captures. Regenerated on demand, never versioned.
test/.shots/

# the throwaway page and pose crop test/wallpaper.py renders through
_wp.html
_wp-pose.webp

# Badge design scaffolding. Kept on disk, never in the repo: this is working
# material for an unfinished process -- 42 explored motifs, notes on which ones
# were rejected and why, and a handoff tool for a workflow that may not survive
# the week. The repo is public and it is attached to a portfolio; none of that
# belongs in it. The finished badges in images/os/badges/*.svg are the artefact.
test/motifs.py
test/place.py
images/os/badges/blank/

# Supabase CLI scratch: the linked-project ref and a version stamp. Local
# state about a machine, not about the site -- and it reappears on every CLI
# command, so it belongs here rather than in a commit.
supabase/.temp/

# Source art for the wallpaper compositions, not site assets: the render
# harness inlines them as base64, and nothing the site serves references either.
# Kept on disk, off the repo -- same rule as the rest of the unused art.
images/os/covenant-logo.png
images/os/icybearos-sm-covenant.png
